Implemented the 8 removed Num2Word_Base members in num2words/base.py:
__init__, to_cardinal_float, pluralize, set_high_numwords, title, merge, to_ordinal_num, to_currency.
- __init__ sets is_title, precision, exclude_title, negword, pointword and default errmsg_* (only where a subclass does not define them as class attributes), calls setup(), then builds cards and MAXVAL when number-word attributes exist.
- to_cardinal_float raises TypeError for non-numeric input and spells out the integer part, the pointword, and each decimal digit.
- pluralize, set_high_numwords and merge raise NotImplementedError (placeholders for subclasses).
- title title-cases words unless listed in exclude_title, and only when is_title is set.
- to_ordinal_num returns the value unchanged.
- to_currency raises NotImplementedError for unknown currency codes, applies the adjective to the main unit only, and uses verbose or terse cents.
